 "slug": "lattice-boards-survey",
 "title": "UP5K and ECP5 boards from awesome-latticeFPGAs: gateware survey",
 "description": "Gateware for the iCE40 UP5K and ECP5 boards of awesome-latticeFPGAs: 20 recommended, all catalogued.",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Status 2026-09-28:** all 20 \"Recommended to clone\" repos are cloned and in `docs/catalogue.md`."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Date: 2026-09-28. Research only. Nothing was cloned into ulx3s-klod."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Source list: `kelu124/awesome-latticeFPGAs` `Readme.md`. The README has a capital R, so `README.md` returns 404. There is\nno data file; the list is hand-written markdown. I kept the sections \"UP5K\", \"ECP5\", \"Conference badges\" and\n\"Other commercial products → UP5K / ECP5\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Excluded: every slug in `.claude/memory/sources.tsv` (for example wuxx__icesugar, osresearch__up5k,\nicebreaker-fpga__*, kbob__icebreaker-candy, smunaut__ice40-playground, damdoy__ice40_ultraplus_examples,\nmachdyne__zeitlos, machdyne__nes_ecp5), all boards and repos in `docs/ecp5-boards-survey.md` (OrangeCrab, LUNA/Cynthion,\niCESugar-Pro, HAD2019, Colorlight, ButterStick, ECPIX-5, Logicbone, Versa/EVN, TinyFPGA EX, IcePi Zero including\nm1nl/icepi-zero-minimig, ECP5-mini, Pergola, basic-ecp5-pcb), and ULX3S/ULX4M."
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Evidence** comes from a tarball file listing (codeload `tar.gz/HEAD`, streamed, not kept) taken on 2026-09-28:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "`V` = verified: a constraint file (`.pcf` for iCE40, `.lpf` for ECP5) and HDL are in the tree. Counts are given as p=pcf, l=lpf, v=.v, sv=.sv.",
    "`U` = unverified: no constraint file seen, the files were not checked, or the only source is the README."
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Toolchain:**"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "\"open\" = a Makefile, .mk or .ys file in the tree calls nextpnr-ice40/icepack or nextpnr-ecp5/ecppack.",
    "\"open?\" = the HDL and pcf/lpf are present but no build file matched. Often the build files sit in a submodule (for example no2build), which the tarball does not include."
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Stars, last push and license come from the GitHub search API on 2026-09-28."
  },
  {
   "type": "hr"
  }
 ],
